{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`, `infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh` claims to prove the current review pipeline but checks only `LLM-Review` before submit. `infra/gerrit/project.config` also requires `Verified`. The script's test commit lacks the required `rebar-ticket:` trailer, so it no longer models an admissible production change.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate the live/manual E2E flow to create a valid ticket-linked commit and wait for both active gate votes before testing submit and replication. Keep credentials secret and cleanup bounded.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test commit carries a resolvable full-canonical `rebar-ticket:` trailer and DCO sign-off.\n- [ ] The E2E fails unless both `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` are present on the tested patchset.\n- [ ] Submit and GitHub-replication assertions run only after both votes pass.\n- [ ] Existing credential-redaction, exit-code, and cleanup contracts remain intact.\n- [ ] Focused tests, shell checks, lint, and typecheck pass.\n\n## Plan-review remediation 2026-09-06\n\nThe CI trigger prerequisite for `Verified +1` is verified in-session with observable proxies, not by relying on a live Gerrit run in unit tests:\n\n- The script's Gerrit polling logic will parse the current patchset's labels and require `Verified.recommended` (or equivalent `+1`) in addition to `LLM-Review +1` before leaving the wait loop.\n- A focused script test will feed stubbed Gerrit change JSON where `LLM-Review` is +1 but `Verified` is absent/0 and assert the E2E does **not** proceed to submit. A second fixture with both labels +1 asserts submit is attempted.\n- A focused static/parser test will assert the generated test commit body contains a resolvable full canonical `rebar-ticket:` trailer plus `Signed-off-by`, using an isolated disposable ticket fixture unless the script is running in the external live integration mode.\n- The live script remains the external integration test: it may create/use a live disposable ticket because the operator ruling allows live-store access only for external integration tests. Non-external tests use stubs/fixtures and must not mutate the live store.\n\nUpdated verification commands:\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" bash -n infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_reviewbot_e2e.py` (or the existing focused test file that owns this script)\n- Safety grep proving the old single-vote wait did not survive: search the script/tests for the submit path and assert both `LLM-Review` and `Verified` gates are present before submit.\n\n\n## Plan-review re-dispatch 2026-09-07 — replicated branch target\n\nEliminate the unreplicated `gerrit-e2e-test` prerequisite. The E2E exercise now targets a replicated `feature/*` branch, e.g. `feature/e2e-gate-smoke`, because `infra/gerrit/replication.config` already replicates `refs/heads/main`, `refs/changes/*`, and `refs/heads/feature/*`. That means the Gerrit-to-platform CI dispatch can observe the branch on the GitHub mirror and cast `Verified` for the review under test.\n\nThe script must create/update the temporary feature branch for the run, use that branch as the test change target, and clean it up after the run by deleting the temporary `feature/e2e-gate-smoke` branch/ref when the exercise completes or fails. If the feature branch cannot be created, observed on the mirror, or deleted during cleanup, the E2E must fail with an explicit harness error naming the branch-replication/cleanup prerequisite rather than waiting forever for `Verified`.\n\nThe live-store isolation ruling remains unchanged: only the external live integration script may create or touch the live disposable ticket/store. Unit and non-external tests must use isolated stubs/fixtures and must not mutate the live store.\n\n\n## Final plan-review amendment 2026-09-07\n\nRepository facts for the focused test target:\n\n- Live E2E script path: `infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh`.\n- Existing sibling E2E script/test precedent: `infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh` is tested by `tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py`.\n- No current test owns `reviewbot-e2e.sh`: repository search for `reviewbot-e2e` under `tests/` returns no matches, and there is no `tests/infra/` directory.\n\nTherefore this change will ADD the focused owner test at exact path `tests/test_reviewbot_e2e.py` (same top-level tests convention as `tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py`), and the verification command is `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/test_reviewbot_e2e.py`. The test owns `infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh` by asserting the generated test commit carries a full canonical `rebar-ticket:` trailer plus DCO, the wait loop requires both `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` before submit, the E2E target is a replicated `feature/e2e-gate-smoke` branch, and cleanup deletes that temporary feature branch.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788784693037057001,"uuid":"473a06ff-78f0-4a99-9c62-764290194ffd"}